WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.549
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:05.667
Sammy.

00:00:06.191 --> 00:00:08.081
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:08.990
Go!

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:11.544
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:13.982
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:14.017 --> 00:00:16.267
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.518
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:19.464 --> 00:00:20.498
This is dad's book.

00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:22.711
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:24.762
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:24.797 --> 00:00:26.490
The family business.

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:27.898
I got to find dad.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:30.472
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:52.288
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:00:52.438 --> 00:00:55.091
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:57.745
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:00.188
So make it count.

00:01:32.989 --> 00:01:34.014
On three.

00:01:34.887 --> 00:01:35.955
One.

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:37.762
Two.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.474
Three.

00:01:43.151 --> 00:01:44.738
Is it still here?

00:01:44.773 --> 00:01:45.888
Okay.

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:47.803
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:01:47.838 --> 00:01:49.470
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:52.938 --> 00:01:54.491
All right, go!

00:01:57.231 --> 00:01:58.683
Sam!

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.480
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:06.515 --> 00:02:07.860
Here, take this!

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.235
Run!

00:02:19.255 --> 00:02:21.663
Come on!

00:02:59.972 --> 00:03:01.491
Dean!

00:03:02.268 --> 00:03:03.147
Dean!

00:03:03.368 --> 00:03:04.256
Hey!

00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:06.599
Hey, hey!

00:03:16.211 --> 00:03:17.742
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:20.115
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.157
Right, um...

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.405
Okay.

00:03:26.865 --> 00:03:30.176
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:32.649 --> 00:03:36.279
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:36.314 --> 00:03:39.286
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:39.321 --> 00:03:42.073
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:03:42.108 --> 00:03:44.826
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:03:44.861 --> 00:03:46.356
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:47.227
Yeah.

00:03:47.262 --> 00:03:49.508
Well, thank god you did.

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:53.045
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:03:53.311 --> 00:03:54.256
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:03:54.291 --> 00:03:56.428
He's resting. And?

00:03:56.463 --> 00:03:58.953
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:03.709
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:06.386
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:09.643
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:09.678 --> 00:04:12.866
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.397
No, no, there is...

00:04:14.432 --> 00:04:17.278
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:19.522
We can't work miracles.

00:04:19.557 --> 00:04:22.200
I really am sorry.

00:04:31.489 --> 00:04:37.107
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:38.757 --> 00:04:40.342
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:40.377 --> 00:04:42.790
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:45.699
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.947
Yeah.

00:04:47.982 --> 00:04:51.743
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:04:51.778 --> 00:04:53.808
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:55.713
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:04:55.748 --> 00:04:57.549
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:04:57.584 --> 00:05:01.551
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.528
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:11.563 --> 00:05:13.976
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:14.011 --> 00:05:16.254
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:19.256
We still have options. What options?

00:05:19.291 --> 00:05:22.154
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:25.017
I know it's not easy.

00:05:26.165 --> 00:05:28.788
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:31.702
And you can't stop it.

00:05:33.695 --> 00:05:35.436
Watch me.

00:05:35.471 --> 00:05:37.935
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.399
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:45.702
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:05:45.737 --> 00:05:48.474
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:52.111
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:05:52.146 --> 00:05:54.064
It's Dean...

00:05:54.099 --> 00:05:56.803
He's sick and uh...

00:05:56.967 --> 00:06:00.588
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:06:01.874 --> 00:06:03.260
But uh...

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:06.278
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:06.313 --> 00:06:08.942
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:08.977 --> 00:06:12.066
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:12.982 --> 00:06:14.460
All right.

00:06:14.495 --> 00:06:16.868
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:31.482 --> 00:06:32.811
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:32.846 --> 00:06:35.818
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:35.853 --> 00:06:39.896
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:42.407
You know, this whole...

00:06:42.442 --> 00:06:44.874
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:06:44.909 --> 00:06:47.199
I can see right through it.

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:49.158
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:06:49.193 --> 00:06:51.389
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:06:51.424 --> 00:06:55.160
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:06:56.737 --> 00:06:59.780
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:06:59.815 --> 00:07:01.608
For what'll help you.

00:07:01.643 --> 00:07:04.699
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:07.271
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:07.306 --> 00:07:09.808
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:09.843 --> 00:07:11.861
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:11.896 --> 00:07:14.380
We're going.

00:07:34.525 --> 00:07:37.642
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:38.945 --> 00:07:41.899
I got you. I got it!

00:07:42.824 --> 00:07:44.756
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:46.855
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.578
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:07:48.613 --> 00:07:50.852
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:07:50.887 --> 00:07:54.322
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:07:54.357 --> 00:07:57.336
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:07:57.371 --> 00:07:59.591
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:07:59.626 --> 00:08:02.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:02.109 --> 00:08:05.513
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:05.548 --> 00:08:07.755
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.176
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:10.211 --> 00:08:12.563
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:12.598 --> 00:08:15.913
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:18.733
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:18.768 --> 00:08:20.966
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:22.548
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:22.583 --> 00:08:24.010
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:24.045 --> 00:08:26.021
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:26.056 --> 00:08:27.319
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:27.354 --> 00:08:28.920
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:28.955 --> 00:08:30.486
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:30.521 --> 00:08:33.307
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:35.950
Maybe he does.

00:08:35.985 --> 00:08:38.265
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.349
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:40.384 --> 00:08:42.477
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:42.512 --> 00:08:44.249
Leila.

00:08:44.284 --> 00:08:47.645
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:51.156
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:08:51.191 --> 00:08:54.446
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:08:54.481 --> 00:08:56.216
Bye.

00:08:56.483 --> 00:08:59.433
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:08:59.468 --> 00:09:01.561
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:09:01.596 --> 00:09:04.889
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:07.204 --> 00:09:10.506
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.222
Come on.

00:09:16.257 --> 00:09:17.561
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:17.596 --> 00:09:18.998
We're sitting up front.

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:20.400
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:20.435 --> 00:09:21.927
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:21.962 --> 00:09:23.384
You're all right?

00:09:23.419 --> 00:09:27.086
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:28.113 --> 00:09:30.096
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:30.131 --> 00:09:32.064
Take it off

00:09:41.786 --> 00:09:46.388
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:09:46.423 --> 00:09:48.939
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:09:48.974 --> 00:09:51.421
Seems like there's always someone

00:09:51.456 --> 00:09:56.863
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:09:56.898 --> 00:09:59.989
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:10:00.024 --> 00:10:01.434
Here, here.

00:10:01.469 --> 00:10:07.987
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:08.022 --> 00:10:12.614
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:12.649 --> 00:10:17.172
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:17.207 --> 00:10:20.788
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:20.823 --> 00:10:23.233
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:23.268 --> 00:10:25.643
You think so young man?

00:10:27.084 --> 00:10:30.503
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:30.538 --> 00:10:35.479
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:38.929
What's your name son?

00:10:39.567 --> 00:10:42.342
Dean. Dean.

00:10:44.083 --> 00:10:47.871
I want you to come up here with me.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.402
No, it's okay.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.690
What are you doing?

00:10:58.725 --> 00:11:02.618
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:04.829 --> 00:11:07.647
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:07.682 --> 00:11:11.623
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:14.123 --> 00:11:18.743
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:20.224 --> 00:11:22.622
Get up there!

00:11:22.851 --> 00:11:26.994
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:33.236 --> 00:11:34.962
You're ready?

00:11:34.997 --> 00:11:37.800
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:37.835 --> 00:11:40.623
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:40.768 --> 00:11:42.653
You will be son.

00:11:42.688 --> 00:11:44.538
You will be.

00:11:44.722 --> 00:11:47.396
Pray with me friends.

00:12:11.068 --> 00:12:15.260
All right now.

00:12:24.258 --> 00:12:26.862
All right now.

00:12:31.311 --> 00:12:33.028
Dean!

00:12:37.885 --> 00:12:39.925
Say something!

00:12:53.256 --> 00:12:55.111
So you really feel okay?

00:12:55.146 --> 00:12:56.464
I feel fine Sam.

00:12:56.499 --> 00:13:00.361
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:13:00.396 --> 00:13:02.121
No sign there ever was.

00:13:02.156 --> 00:13:05.888
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:05.923 --> 00:13:07.902
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:07.937 --> 00:13:09.063
What do you mean strange?

00:13:09.098 --> 00:13:12.711
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:12.746 --> 00:13:15.414
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:16.255 --> 00:13:18.053
Thanks doc.

00:13:18.088 --> 00:13:19.851
No problem.

00:13:21.006 --> 00:13:23.112
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:23.147 --> 00:13:25.267
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:25.302 --> 00:13:27.352
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:27.387 --> 00:13:30.021
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:30.056 --> 00:13:32.787
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:32.822 --> 00:13:34.739
What feeling?

00:13:34.774 --> 00:13:38.204
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:38.239 --> 00:13:41.510
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:41.545 --> 00:13:43.429
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:13:43.464 --> 00:13:45.278
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:13:45.313 --> 00:13:47.922
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:13:47.957 --> 00:13:50.150
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:13:50.185 --> 00:13:51.899
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:13:51.934 --> 00:13:54.865
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:59.042
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:14:01.347 --> 00:14:03.334
Yeah, right.

00:14:04.406 --> 00:14:06.649
So what do you want to do?

00:14:06.684 --> 00:14:08.061
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:08.096 --> 00:14:10.292
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:13.221 --> 00:14:14.814
I feel great.

00:14:14.849 --> 00:14:16.372
Just trying to...

00:14:16.407 --> 00:14:18.488
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:18.523 --> 00:14:21.415
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:21.794 --> 00:14:26.321
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:27.014 --> 00:14:29.623
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:29.658 --> 00:14:32.197
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:32.232 --> 00:14:36.564
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:36.599 --> 00:14:38.157
So uh...

00:14:38.192 --> 00:14:40.448
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:40.483 --> 00:14:43.063
I was weak but...

00:14:43.098 --> 00:14:46.492
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:14:46.527 --> 00:14:48.064
I went into a coma.

00:14:48.099 --> 00:14:50.898
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:14:50.933 --> 00:14:53.398
And the cancer was gone.

00:14:53.433 --> 00:14:59.095
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:01.804
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:15:01.839 --> 00:15:04.412
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:04.447 --> 00:15:06.950
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:06.985 --> 00:15:12.520
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:14.156 --> 00:15:16.372
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:16.407 --> 00:15:18.641
Of course you can.

00:15:19.333 --> 00:15:21.893
Why? Why me?

00:15:21.928 --> 00:15:25.279
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:25.314 --> 00:15:29.090
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:29.125 --> 00:15:36.541
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:36.705 --> 00:15:40.332
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:40.367 --> 00:15:44.126
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:15:44.161 --> 00:15:47.183
And it isn't finished.

00:15:48.908 --> 00:15:53.003
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:15:53.038 --> 00:15:55.899
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:15:55.934 --> 00:15:58.760
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:15:58.795 --> 00:16:00.672
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:16:00.707 --> 00:16:02.418
Said that something was...

00:16:02.453 --> 00:16:04.095
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:07.783
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:09.854
All right, thanks.

00:16:12.309 --> 00:16:13.783
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:13.818 --> 00:16:15.291
You're clock's busted.

00:16:15.326 --> 00:16:16.730
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:16.765 --> 00:16:21.236
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:21.271 --> 00:16:23.839
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:23.874 --> 00:16:25.731
How did you know?

00:16:29.209 --> 00:16:31.756
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:31.953 --> 00:16:33.659
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:33.694 --> 00:16:36.091
Cured, I guess.

00:16:36.126 --> 00:16:37.689
What are you doing here?

00:16:37.724 --> 00:16:40.953
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:40.988 --> 00:16:42.704
Leila.

00:16:43.738 --> 00:16:47.858
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:16:47.893 --> 00:16:50.284
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:16:50.319 --> 00:16:52.320
Sue Ann please.

00:16:52.355 --> 00:16:54.998
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:16:55.033 --> 00:16:57.213
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:16:57.248 --> 00:17:00.367
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:17:00.402 --> 00:17:03.694
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.413
Why are you still even here?

00:17:13.448 --> 00:17:15.502
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:15.537 --> 00:17:17.365
Stop.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.976
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:20.011 --> 00:17:22.491
We've been to every single service.

00:17:22.526 --> 00:17:25.441
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:25.476 --> 00:17:28.639
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:28.674 --> 00:17:31.802
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:31.837 --> 00:17:34.448
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:36.652 --> 00:17:38.944
I have this thing.

00:17:38.979 --> 00:17:41.236
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:41.691 --> 00:17:44.636
It's inoperable.

00:17:44.812 --> 00:17:48.547
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:17:52.982 --> 00:17:55.217
I'm sorry.

00:17:55.751 --> 00:17:57.651
It's okay.

00:17:57.686 --> 00:17:59.666
No.

00:17:59.952 --> 00:18:02.667
It isn't.

00:18:07.865 --> 00:18:12.278
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:40.652 --> 00:18:42.991
What did you find out?

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.631
I'm sorry.

00:18:45.819 --> 00:18:47.010
Sorry about what?

00:18:47.045 --> 00:18:52.579
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:18:52.797 --> 00:18:55.285
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:58.863
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:18:58.898 --> 00:19:02.509
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:02.544 --> 00:19:05.245
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.666
And each time the victim died

00:19:06.701 --> 00:19:09.572
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:09.607 --> 00:19:12.443
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:12.478 --> 00:19:15.849
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:16.033 --> 00:19:20.226
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:21.397 --> 00:19:23.101
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:23.136 --> 00:19:25.713
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:25.748 --> 00:19:27.642
Dean...

00:19:27.856 --> 00:19:30.282
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:30.317 --> 00:19:32.708
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:34.862 --> 00:19:37.230
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:37.265 --> 00:19:39.814
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:39.849 --> 00:19:42.363
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:19:42.398 --> 00:19:45.172
I didn't know.

00:19:46.008 --> 00:19:49.015
Pray with me friends.

00:19:49.857 --> 00:19:53.046
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:19:53.081 --> 00:19:55.892
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:19:55.927 --> 00:19:58.674
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:19:58.819 --> 00:20:00.949
Something else is doing it for him.

00:20:00.984 --> 00:20:05.268
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:05.658 --> 00:20:07.456
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:07.491 --> 00:20:09.549
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:09.584 --> 00:20:13.946
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:13.981 --> 00:20:16.613
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:16.521 --> 00:21:18.282
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:18.317 --> 00:21:21.303
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:21.338 --> 00:21:23.829
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:23.864 --> 00:21:26.180
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:26.215 --> 00:21:27.949
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:27.984 --> 00:21:29.932
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:29.967 --> 00:21:31.845
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:35.845
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:38.731
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:39.635 --> 00:21:41.669
Reapers stop time.

00:21:41.704 --> 00:21:43.190
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:21:43.225 --> 00:21:45.247
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:21:45.282 --> 00:21:47.234
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:21:47.269 --> 00:21:50.499
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:21:50.534 --> 00:21:52.190
That cross.

00:21:52.225 --> 00:21:54.624
What? There was this cross.

00:21:54.659 --> 00:21:59.236
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:04.961 --> 00:22:06.812
Here.

00:22:07.356 --> 00:22:08.461
Tarot?

00:22:08.496 --> 00:22:10.046
It makes sense.

00:22:10.081 --> 00:22:12.232
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:12.267 --> 00:22:13.998
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:14.033 --> 00:22:15.694
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:15.729 --> 00:22:19.905
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:22.791
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:22.826 --> 00:22:24.986
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:25.021 --> 00:22:28.942
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:35.083 --> 00:22:37.826
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:37.861 --> 00:22:38.831
You know how?

00:22:38.866 --> 00:22:40.265
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:42.113
We can't kill Roy.

00:22:42.148 --> 00:22:43.301
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:22:43.336 --> 00:22:45.953
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:22:45.988 --> 00:22:48.853
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:22:48.888 --> 00:22:50.782
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:22:50.817 --> 00:22:53.601
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:22:53.636 --> 00:22:56.684
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:22:56.975 --> 00:22:58.306
Okay, uh...

00:22:58.341 --> 00:23:00.721
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:23:00.756 --> 00:23:03.149
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:03.184 --> 00:23:05.713
And how to break it.

00:23:10.799 --> 00:23:14.025
Service today.

00:23:18.777 --> 00:23:21.415
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:22.617
See if you can find it.

00:23:22.652 --> 00:23:25.481
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:25.516 --> 00:23:28.259
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:28.294 --> 00:23:29.961
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:29.996 --> 00:23:31.650
Thank you.

00:24:28.478 --> 00:24:30.770
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:24:57.334 --> 00:25:02.934
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:13.058 --> 00:25:16.316
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:25.843 --> 00:25:26.726
What have you got?

00:25:26.761 --> 00:25:28.751
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:28.786 --> 00:25:30.706
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:30.741 --> 00:25:32.755
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:32.790 --> 00:25:34.814
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:34.849 --> 00:25:37.795
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:25:58.410 --> 00:25:59.346
Leila.

00:25:59.381 --> 00:26:02.606
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:07.896 --> 00:26:09.898
Mom... Baby.

00:26:09.933 --> 00:26:11.900
I love you.

00:26:12.950 --> 00:26:15.042
Oh, man.

00:26:24.169 --> 00:26:26.846
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:26.881 --> 00:26:28.824
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:28.859 --> 00:26:30.623
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:30.658 --> 00:26:32.671
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:32.706 --> 00:26:34.649
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:34.684 --> 00:26:37.890
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:37.925 --> 00:26:41.096
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:41.131 --> 00:26:43.295
Please...

00:26:51.560 --> 00:26:52.972
I'm sorry.

00:26:53.007 --> 00:26:54.875
Leila. Leila!

00:26:54.910 --> 00:26:56.743
Dear child.

00:26:57.834 --> 00:27:01.019
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:27:01.054 --> 00:27:03.952
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:07.421 --> 00:27:09.286
Help!

00:27:16.366 --> 00:27:18.717
Pray with me friends.

00:27:22.804 --> 00:27:25.889
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:36.165 --> 00:27:37.506
Help!

00:27:37.541 --> 00:27:38.899
Help me please!

00:27:38.934 --> 00:27:40.257
Where is it?

00:27:40.472 --> 00:27:42.724
It's right there!

00:27:44.157 --> 00:27:46.169
Come on, come on.

00:27:54.920 --> 00:27:56.390
Fire!

00:27:56.425 --> 00:27:58.996
The tent's on fire!

00:27:59.144 --> 00:28:01.131
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:28:01.166 --> 00:28:03.716
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:03.751 --> 00:28:05.864
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:05.899 --> 00:28:07.840
Reverend, please!

00:28:07.875 --> 00:28:09.781
Please don't stop.

00:28:09.816 --> 00:28:11.400
Please.

00:28:11.435 --> 00:28:12.950
Friends.

00:28:12.985 --> 00:28:16.561
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:16.596 --> 00:28:19.269
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:19.304 --> 00:28:22.161
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:22.196 --> 00:28:25.018
David? I think its okay.

00:28:28.768 --> 00:28:30.378
No!

00:28:30.413 --> 00:28:31.605
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:33.626
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:34.600 --> 00:28:36.143
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:36.178 --> 00:28:38.777
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:38.812 --> 00:28:41.305
Then who the hell is?

00:28:44.356 --> 00:28:46.469
Sue Ann.

00:29:00.611 --> 00:29:02.903
Help! Help me!

00:29:03.047 --> 00:29:04.837
Help!

00:29:19.268 --> 00:29:21.591
I got you. I got you.

00:29:24.134 --> 00:29:26.118
Thank god.

00:29:31.398 --> 00:29:34.433
I just don't understand.

00:29:34.468 --> 00:29:36.231
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:36.266 --> 00:29:39.358
After Roy healed you.

00:29:40.312 --> 00:29:44.658
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:29:45.994 --> 00:29:48.467
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:29:48.502 --> 00:29:53.656
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:29:55.401 --> 00:29:56.976
We catch you around here again son.

00:29:57.011 --> 00:29:59.727
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:29:59.762 --> 00:30:01.494
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:30:01.529 --> 00:30:03.348
Got it.

00:30:06.400 --> 00:30:07.932
Leila.

00:30:08.621 --> 00:30:10.244
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:10.279 --> 00:30:12.574
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:12.609 --> 00:30:14.551
He's not a healer.

00:30:14.586 --> 00:30:16.493
He healed you.

00:30:18.131 --> 00:30:20.174
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:20.209 --> 00:30:24.808
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:26.787 --> 00:30:29.293
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:33.870 --> 00:30:37.839
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:37.874 --> 00:30:40.451
Same to you.

00:30:44.427 --> 00:30:47.721
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:30:51.074 --> 00:30:53.539
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:30:53.574 --> 00:30:56.004
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:30:56.039 --> 00:30:59.530
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:03.640 --> 00:31:06.913
So Roy really believes.

00:31:07.452 --> 00:31:10.101
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:10.136 --> 00:31:14.308
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:14.343 --> 00:31:17.604
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:17.639 --> 00:31:19.678
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:19.713 --> 00:31:21.502
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:21.537 --> 00:31:23.889
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:23.924 --> 00:31:27.148
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:27.183 --> 00:31:30.637
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:30.672 --> 00:31:34.132
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:34.167 --> 00:31:38.676
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:38.711 --> 00:31:40.480
Desperate.

00:31:40.515 --> 00:31:43.788
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:31:43.823 --> 00:31:47.061
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:31:47.096 --> 00:31:50.701
Cheating death. Literally.

00:31:50.736 --> 00:31:54.110
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:31:54.145 --> 00:31:59.651
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:32:00.655 --> 00:32:04.116
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:04.151 --> 00:32:07.714
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:09.928 --> 00:32:12.325
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:12.360 --> 00:32:14.687
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:14.722 --> 00:32:17.599
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:17.634 --> 00:32:19.578
Maybe both?

00:32:20.610 --> 00:32:23.025
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:23.060 --> 00:32:26.021
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:37.866 --> 00:32:39.742
That's Leila's car.

00:32:39.777 --> 00:32:41.618
She's already here.

00:32:41.653 --> 00:32:43.405
Yeah.

00:32:44.166 --> 00:32:46.907
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:32:46.942 --> 00:32:49.067
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:32:49.102 --> 00:32:51.385
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:53.813
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:32:53.848 --> 00:32:56.172
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:32:56.207 --> 00:33:00.518
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:33:00.553 --> 00:33:05.183
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:19.034 --> 00:33:20.071
Gather around.

00:33:20.106 --> 00:33:22.259
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:22.294 --> 00:33:24.412
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:24.447 --> 00:33:26.704
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:27.129 --> 00:33:29.144
House.

00:33:29.956 --> 00:33:31.464
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:31.499 --> 00:33:32.981
What are you...

00:33:34.363 --> 00:33:36.013
Hey.

00:33:36.723 --> 00:33:40.099
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:23.751 --> 00:34:25.534
See him?

00:34:25.858 --> 00:34:27.692
Na.

00:34:48.661 --> 00:34:51.086
Psycho mutt.

00:35:36.433 --> 00:35:40.579
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:35:52.132 --> 00:35:54.042
Sam, can't you see?

00:35:54.077 --> 00:35:55.917
The Lord chose me.

00:35:55.952 --> 00:35:58.687
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:35:58.722 --> 00:36:01.070
And your brother is wicked.

00:36:01.105 --> 00:36:05.485
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:05.520 --> 00:36:08.219
That's god's will.

00:36:10.429 --> 00:36:12.948
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:17.014 --> 00:36:18.700
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:18.735 --> 00:36:20.909
You pray with me now.

00:36:20.944 --> 00:36:23.084
Pray with me friends.

00:36:52.225 --> 00:36:54.298
All right now.

00:36:55.361 --> 00:36:58.187
All right now.

00:37:23.927 --> 00:37:25.857
All right.

00:37:51.370 --> 00:37:56.587
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:37:57.425 --> 00:37:58.495
My god!

00:37:58.530 --> 00:38:00.449
What have you done?

00:38:00.484 --> 00:38:02.368
He's not your god.

00:38:02.403 --> 00:38:04.407
Reverend?

00:38:04.442 --> 00:38:06.412
Sue Ann?

00:38:52.727 --> 00:38:54.444
You okay?

00:38:54.732 --> 00:38:56.801
A little bit weak.

00:38:56.836 --> 00:38:58.472
Yeah.

00:38:59.674 --> 00:39:01.534
All right, come on.

00:39:01.569 --> 00:39:03.394
We should get going.

00:39:14.740 --> 00:39:16.834
What is it?

00:39:16.869 --> 00:39:18.928
Nothing.

00:39:20.307 --> 00:39:21.585
What is it?

00:39:21.620 --> 00:39:23.550
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:23.585 --> 00:39:25.618
Of course we did.

00:39:25.653 --> 00:39:27.975
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:29.073 --> 00:39:30.784
I got it.

00:39:34.610 --> 00:39:38.005
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:38.040 --> 00:39:39.916
Hey.

00:39:40.762 --> 00:39:42.570
How did you know we were here?

00:39:42.605 --> 00:39:44.461
Sam called.

00:39:44.496 --> 00:39:48.242
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:39:48.409 --> 00:39:51.423
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:39:56.143 --> 00:39:58.268
So um...

00:39:58.303 --> 00:40:01.484
Where are you going?

00:40:01.519 --> 00:40:02.690
Don't know yet.

00:40:02.725 --> 00:40:06.769
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:08.499 --> 00:40:12.863
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:12.898 --> 00:40:15.527
What happened?

00:40:16.756 --> 00:40:19.068
Nothing.

00:40:19.290 --> 00:40:25.313
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:25.348 --> 00:40:27.907
I'm sorry.

00:40:28.091 --> 00:40:30.670
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:30.705 --> 00:40:32.642
And Sue Ann...

00:40:32.677 --> 00:40:34.342
She's dead, you know?

00:40:34.377 --> 00:40:36.292
A stroke.

00:40:36.327 --> 00:40:39.411
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:40.068 --> 00:40:43.210
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:40:43.383 --> 00:40:46.614
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:51.845
Must be ruff...

00:40:51.880 --> 00:40:54.250
To believe in something so much.

00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:57.665
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:41:01.801 --> 00:41:05.103
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:06.304 --> 00:41:11.131
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:11.166 --> 00:41:13.525
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:16.703
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:16.738 --> 00:41:21.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:26.628 --> 00:41:30.077
So what now?

00:41:32.489 --> 00:41:36.977
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:41.107 --> 00:41:43.479
Goodbye Dean.

00:41:45.207 --> 00:41:46.923
Hey.

00:41:52.176 --> 00:41:57.269
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:41:58.137 --> 00:42:01.611
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:02.769 --> 00:42:05.118
Well...

00:42:05.284 --> 00:42:08.769
There's a miracle right there.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
